    description: "WHAT. PR #2198 made the node id's kind slot equal Symbol.kind in fennel, gleam, hack, haxe, janet, odin, prisma, tcl and v_lang, and left the stable-id inputs alone: compute_stable_id / scoped_stable_id are still called with fn, var, proc, model, struct, union, type_alias. robot (test_case on kind test) and twig (function_call on kind call_site) mint the node id and the stable id from one word through make_doc_symbol_ids, so there even the node id was left (declared in check_id_construction.KNOWN_KIND_SLOT_HOLES; measured: correcting the word moves 2 of 2 stable ids for each).\n\nASK (owner decision for the v15 bump). Whether the bump corrects the hashed word, and for robot and twig also the id. Not sized: churn per language on a corpus.\n\nALSO. Symbol.kind may itself be wrong where the id's word is a registered kind and the Symbol's is not the closer one: gleam type / type_alias on class / type, odin struct / union on class, v_lang struct on class. Found during PR 1 of the stable-id plan, 2026-11-15 (PR #2198). Detail: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/stable_id_items_review_11152026/pr1/STATUS.md."  # 2144
